{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_min_at_q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_min_at_q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity.lean#L112-L126","doc":"At `q > 1`, the **minimum** eigenvalue of `σ_k² = L_H` is `(q²)⁻¹`\n(since `q² > 1 > (q²)⁻¹`).  This identifies the empirical\n+0.811653754... value measured in\n`binding_link_psd_feasibility_probe.py` as `q_0⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_pos","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity.lean#L101-L110","doc":"For any `q > 0`, both eigenvalues of `σ_k²` in the Hoefsmit\nstandard-(2,1) representation are strictly positive.  This is\nthe categorical strengthening of the numerical PSD-feasibility\nfinding for the Hopf link at q_0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_snd","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity.lean#L95-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig_fst","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity.lean#L85-L93","doc":"Squaring `(+q, −q⁻¹)` componentwise gives `(q², (q²)⁻¹)`.\nStated separately for the first and second components for\nrobustness across Mathlib versions (the second uses\n`(-q⁻¹)² = q⁻² = (q²)⁻¹`, which different Mathlib editions\nnormalise to slightly different canonical forms). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hopfLinkStandardEig","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity.lean#L77-L83","doc":"`σ_k² = L_H` (Hopf link) in the Hoefsmit standard-(2,1)\nrepresentation has eigenvalues `(q², (q²)⁻¹)`.  Squaring the\ndiagonal `(+q, −q⁻¹)` yields `(q², q⁻²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitStandardEig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitStandardEig","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingLinkEigenvalueIdentity.lean#L66-L75","doc":"The two eigenvalues of `σ_k` in the Hoefsmit standard-(2,1)\nrepresentation at parameter `q`: `+q` and `−q⁻¹`.\n\nPer Hoefsmit (1979) §3 / Geck-Pfeiffer (2000) §5: the\nseminormal generators of `H_n(q)` in the (n−1, 1) standard rep\nare diagonal on the basis indexed by reverse standard Young\ntableaux of shape `(n−1, 1)`.  For n=3 this gives a 2×2 diagonal\nmatrix with diagonal `(+q, −q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}